---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

// Public contact for privacy requests. Left empty until the owner supplies one.
const CONTACT_EMAIL = '';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What Desi Alternatives collects, why, who handles it, and how to ask us to change or delete it."
  updated="11 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    This page explains what data Desi Alternatives collects when you use the site, why we collect it, and what
    you can do about it. We try to collect as little as we can.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account details.</strong> Your email address and name when you register or sign in. We sign you in with a one-time code sent to your email, so there is no password.</li>
    <li><strong>Things you submit.</strong> Tool suggestions, ownership claims (including a work email), edit requests and reviews, along with the text you write.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter.</strong> Your email address if you subscribe.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage data.</strong> Pages viewed, searches, outbound clicks, and rough device details such as browser and operating system.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To run your account and keep you signed in.</li>
    <li>To review tool listings, claims and reviews before they go live.</li>
    <li>To send the emails you asked for, such as sign-in codes and the newsletter.</li>
    <li>To see which pages are useful and fix what is not.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell your data.</p>

  <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We use our own page-view counting on Cloudflare, and a cookieless analytics script. Visitors are counted
    with a hashed identifier that changes daily, so we cannot follow one person across days.
  </p>
  <p>
    Google Tag Manager and Google tags are switched off until you press <em>Allow all</em> in the cookie
    banner. If you press <em>Decline</em>, they stay off. Your choice is saved in your browser. A sign-in
    cookie is set when you log in, because the site cannot work without it.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else handles your data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the site, the database and image storage.</li>
    <li><strong>Resend</strong> delivers our emails.</li>
    <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> serves our fonts, so your browser contacts Google when a page loads.</li>
    <li><strong>DiceBear</strong> generates the default profile picture if you have not uploaded one.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023, you can ask to see the data we hold about you,
    correct it, or have it deleted. You can unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time using the link in any
    issue.
  </p>
  {CONTACT_EMAIL && (
    <p>
      To make a request, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> from the address on your
      account.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Account and newsletter data stays until you ask us to remove it. Published reviews and tool listings stay
    on the site unless they are removed.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, the date at the top of the page changes with it.</p>
</LegalLayout>
